{
  "format": "shaderlab-conformance-core",
  "version": 1,
  "subject": "WebGPU preparation of compiled v9 materials: std140 uniform layout, texture/sampler bindings and roles, uniform packing",
  "notes": [
    "Local proposal from the naga spike (docs/materials-platform/NAGA_SPIKE.md); not a WebGPU or TruAPI contract.",
    "Input: parse the canonical text, compile it as a Shaderlab v9 source module (normal or floatLinearFallback variant), then prepare both stages with the given floatFilterable.",
    "Fragment block (group 0, binding 0) order: sl_time, sl_tilt, sl_resolution, sl_orientation, sl_rotation; then each non-sampler parameter as p_<name> in declaration order; then, in the fallback variant only, int _shaderlab_sampling_r_input, _shaderlab_sampling_sp_<name> per sampler parameter and, when the fallback helpers receive r_base with a literal mode, int _shaderlab_sampling_r_base replacing those literals. Vertex block (group 1, binding 0): _shaderlab_target_flip.",
    "std140 rules used (equal to WGSL uniform layout for these types): float and int align 4, size 4; vec2 align 8, size 8; vec3 align 16, size 12 (a following 4-byte scalar packs at offset+12); vec4 align 16, size 16; mat3 align 16, three columns of 16 bytes, size 48. Each member starts at its alignment after the previous end; block size is the last end rounded up to 16.",
    "Textures (group 0) in declaration order r_base, r_input, r_noise, then sp_<name> per sampler parameter; each takes binding 2k+1 for texture2D <name> and 2k+2 for sampler <name>_sampler. Samplers follow the role: noise nearest/repeat with a non-filtering sampler; base, input and arguments linear/clamp-to-edge. byte = 8-bit contents; float = 32-bit float contents (null when the role is always 8-bit). Without float32-filterable, float contents bind unfilterable-float with a non-filtering nearest sampler and the fallback mode uniform is written 1 (0 for byte contents). WebGPU checks texture/sampler pairs across all call sites of a fallback helper, so in a stage that passes float data through the helpers, 8-bit textures with a mode uniform (including r_base) also bind with `float` and mode 1, interpolated in the shader.",
    "pack.expectHex: the whole block, little-endian f32 (i32 for int), mat3 column-major with 4 padding bytes per column, starting from a zeroed buffer; computed independently with Python struct.pack. Error codes are stable; messages are not."
  ],
